<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">François Martin (governor of Pondicherry)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1634–<a href="/years/1706">1706</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">François Martin was an agent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-east-india-company">French East India Company</a> who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pondicherry">Pondicherry</a> in 1674 on land granted by the governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a>. He built up the settlement as the Company's chief base in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, lost it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in 1693 and resumed control when it was returned in 1699, serving as its governor until his death.</p></div>
